A||N||6||Little Duce Coupe||Head light question.....(sigh..so typical eh..)||||5||
Z||000000||Little Duce Coupe||11-14-2001||03:51 PM||||I have an 88 coupe.<P>My left front headlight will not come up by itself.  It winks a lot up and down and every now and then will catch the right spot in the gear and go up.  It is possible for me to lift the cover by hand and then the headlight will come up and stay up.  To date I have never had to use the manual knob, and it will go down by itself every time but VERY hard when it does.<P>Is this something I can fix by swapping a gear out.. or... do I have to replace the entire motor assmbly?<P>I have heard that 88's are easier when it comes to headlight motors.....<P>Please say its true.<P>Thanks in advance for any help.<P>------------------<BR>Little Duce Coupe<BR>"You Don't Know What She Costs"||||reg||5
Z||000001||Fat Frank||11-14-2001||04:17 PM||||I had what sounds like the same thing happen to me except it was the right side. I removed the motor/gearbox and when I got inside,the three plastic cylinders were all ground up.Some of the nice folks on this site told me that Rodney sells what I need.I had to take the motor loose to get the plastic gear out to get to the cylinders and when I did the brushes pop out.Almost lost one of the brush springs so watch for them.<P>||||reg||1
Z||000002||MinnGreenGT||11-14-2001||04:33 PM||||Yup! Frank is correct.  Sounds like you just need Rodney's replacement delrin bushings.  They're <B>really</B> easy to replace (did mine a few months ago). <BR> <A HREF="http://www.rodneydickman.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.rodneydickman.com</A> <P>------------------<BR>              <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/GreenGT6.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000003||StuGood||11-14-2001||06:18 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Little Duce Coupe:<B>I have heard that 88's are easier when it comes to headlight motors.....<BR>Please say its true.<BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE>It's true.  Now, feel better?  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"> <P>Seriously, when a 1987-later Fiero starts to wink at you when you turn the headlights on, it's dropping you a hint.  It's saying, "It'll soon be rebuild time for me... and take care of my sister (the other headlight motor) while you're at it, please."  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> <BR>||||reg||12
Z||000004||Fierobruiser||11-14-2001||09:40 PM||||It's a real easy rebuild. Takes as much time to get the lights out of the car as it does to rebuild them. When you open them up,it's powdered plastic time.<P>------------------<BR>Notchbacks Rule<BR>85GT(show car)<BR>88Coupe (daily driver)<BR>84 Coupe(project car)||||reg||1
Z||000005||cadaver||11-14-2001||09:50 PM||||I have done a few but I made the bushings from aluminum.||||reg||1
Z||000006||Little Duce Coupe||11-15-2001||11:15 AM||||Thanks Everybody for the advice.<P>Think I will give it a shot.<P>I like the aluminum idea, I work where I can get access to someone who can help me do it all I need is one good set of gears from the right side motors for a pattern.<P>Thnks again!<P>Cliff......Thread dead, this grasshopper has learned much.<P>------------------<BR>Little Duce Coupe<BR>"You Don't Know What She Costs"||||reg||7
